# Pin important chats

Help the user keep valuable Agent chats easy to find later.

## When to recommend pinning

Near the end of a useful session (or when the user says they will archive), recommend pinning if the chat has any of:

1. A finished setup or config change (rules, theme, deploy, env).
2. A decision the user may need again (architecture, safety, milestone choice).
3. A working fix that was hard to find (bug + solution).
4. A checklist or runbook the user will reuse.

Do **not** recommend pinning for short Q&A, failed experiments, or one-off typos.

## How to recommend (short)

One short line only, for example:

- *This chat looks worth pinning (setup + decisions). Pin it before you archive.*

If the user is about to archive, remind once:

- *Pin first if you want this later — then archive.*

## How the user pins (manual — Cursor UI)

1. Open the Agents / chat history sidebar.
2. Find this chat.
3. Use **Pin** (or the pin icon / context menu) so it stays at the top.
4. Optional: rename the chat to a clear title (e.g. `Rules: English + stay-on-task`).

## Easy triggers (pick one)

### A — Manual phrase (simplest)

User types in chat:

- `pin this`
- `/pin-chat`

Agent then: confirm why it is worth pinning + give the 3 UI steps above. Do not invent a pin API if none exists.

### B — End-of-goal habit

When the session goal is done and the user says they will archive, agent auto-adds the one-line pin reminder (see above).

### C — Title convention

If the user asks to rename, suggest a short title:

`[Area]: [result]`

Examples: `Theme: GitHub Dark Dimmed`, `verify.sh: Windows python fix`.

## Limits

- One reminder per chat is enough — do not nag every message.
- Never block archiving; only recommend pin first.
